meta {
  name: Clone OPD Tests
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/opd-master-data/{{opdMasterDataId}}/opd-tests/clone
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "targetOPDMasterDataId": "{{targetOPDMasterDataId}}"
  }
}

vars:pre-request {
  targetOPDMasterDataId: 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
}

docs {
  OPD equivalent of the lab **Clone Lab Tests** endpoint (POST /opd-master-data/:masterDataId/opd-tests/clone).
  
  🔒 **RBAC:** requires `business_admin:master_data__duplicate_test` — enforced by `PermissionGuard` (`@RequirePermission`). A caller whose effective permissions (user override ?? branch-role override ?? role baseline) lack this get **403 `PERMISSION_DENIED`**; the `business_admin` / `administrator` roles bypass all checks, so `{{businessAccessToken}}` (an admin) still succeeds here.
  
  Deep-clone all active lab tests from this master data (the `:opdMasterDataId` in
  the URL, the *source*) into a target master data. Each test plus its samples,
  result parameters, and reference ranges/values is copied with fresh ids, the
  target's `branchId`, and a fresh `versionHistory` v1. Returns
  `{ "copied": <n>, "skipped": <n> }`.
  
  A source test is **skipped** if its `testName` or `testCode` already exists
  (active) in the target. Both master data must belong to the caller's tenant
  (404 `MASTER_DATA_NOT_FOUND` otherwise).
  
  Set `targetOPDMasterDataId` to a second (usually different-branch) master data's
  id — create one via Master Data → Create, or grab another from List. The
  placeholder default will 404 until you set a real id.
}
